# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
#
# RDR-2 and RDR-3: F1 opens the prompt, digits go into it, Return opens
# the entry they name. The assertion is confinement, not content: what
# the panel *says* is RDR-1's business in the unit suite, and what a
# person looks at once is the contact sheet (`scripts/frames.py sheet`).
about F1 opens the prompt, and what it draws stays in the panel
kind pair
program START.EXE
store tests/visual/reader-store.txt
both code-wheel
seam journal
until 240000000
every 25
# A screen may appear in the two runs a dump apart, because claiming a
# keystroke changes when the program does its own next repaint by less
# than the gap between two stills. One dump of slack, measured (#234).
slack 1

# Leg 9's prefix: past the code wheel, load slot A, party on the street.
key A@7601
key Return@7651
key L@8951
key A@9201
# The prompt, then entry three.
key F1@10600
key 3@10700
key Return@10800

rect panel 136,8,311,119
rect notes 273,192,311,199

# Before the bar is drawn at all the two runs are the same machine.
allow 0-9000 none
# From the adventuring screen the splice is on the bar and nothing else
# differs until F1 is pressed.
allow 9025-10599 notes
# And from F1 on, the panel too, and still nothing else.
allow 10600-end panel notes
